  "description": "Two items landed. topbar-shell replaced the starter sidebar and unblocked the seven items waiting on it; reviewing it turned up that asserting a plain member sees no Settings link proves only that a link is not rendered, so tests were added against the destination itself. A mutation entry for that guard was written and then withdrawn: the destination is guarded twice and independently, by the route middleware and by PropertyDefinitions::mount, so removing either leaves the other refusing and the test still passes -- an entry takes one remove string, so none can prove either guard, and recording one would have asserted exactly the false confidence the mutation rule exists to prevent. name-key then settled the comparison question content-actions had been blocking on, and its first attempt failed on MySQL alone with errno 1553, having dropped a composite index that was silently carrying a foreign key. Diagnosis waited for the log rather than acting on a guess about lockForUpdate, which was wrong; the 410-second run that looked like a hang was 415 tests each re-running the failing migration. Both PHPStan and Pint also rejected the first fix for the annotation that made name_key visible to static analysis, and a CI workflow auto-applied Pint mid-review, so its commit was kept and the cleaner form applied on top rather than force-pushed over."
}
